Say which step of distillation the browser died on.

Tapping reader mode on an article killed the browser process with
SIGTRAP(TRAP_BRKPT) on CrBrowserMain. The dump could not be symbolised: the
library ships without symbols, so the report is addresses and a note that the
unwinder gave up and guessed the rest of the stack by scanning it.

The trap instruction itself can be read out of the disassembly. It is one of a
pair -- one for "argument <= 0", one for "argument >= 12" -- guarding a call,
which is the shape a compiler gives a two-sided bounds check on an enum with
twelve values. That says what went wrong in the abstract and nothing about
where, and the stack below the trap is not trustworthy enough to say more.

So the path announces itself: every call MaybeStartDistillation and
StartNavigationToDistillerViewer make is preceded by a line naming it. The last
line before the process dies is the call that trapped. The macro is a no-op off
HarmonyOS and comes out once the answer is in.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after chromium-154-harmonyos.patch.

