 namespace {
 
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_OHOS)
+// TEMPORARY. Tapping reader mode killed the browser process with SIGTRAP and
+// the crash dump could not be symbolised -- the library is built without
+// symbols, so the report gave addresses and nothing else. What could be read
+// out of the disassembly is that the trap is a two-sided bounds check on a
+// small integer argument, valid range 1..11, which is the shape of an enum
+// with twelve values arriving as zero. That narrows it very little on its own,
+// so each step of the path says it is about to happen. The last line in the
+// log before the process dies is the call that did it.
+#define OHOS_DISTILL_STEP(what) LOG(WARNING) << "OHOS reader mode: " << (what)
+#else
+#define OHOS_DISTILL_STEP(what) \
+  do {                          \
+  } while (false)
+#endif
